    "summary": "High‑energy show with soaring Other One suite and crisp Mexicali Blues",
    "blurb": "The November 14 1971 TCU concert delivers a blistering Other One > Me And My Uncle > Other One sequence, tight Mexican blues leads and an inspired Sugar Magnolia. Jerry’s youthful tone and Phil’s thumping bass drive the set while the soundboard capture is crystal‑clear. A top‑tier performance for anyone chasing early‑’71 fire.",
    "review": "The Dead bring their A‑game to Texas Christian University on November 14, 1971, kicking off with a punchy first set that moves from Bertha and Beat It On Down The Line into a fluid China Cat > I Know You Rider segue. Highlights include a fiery Mexicali Blues where Jerry’s lead is both cosmic and razor‑sharp, and a tight, sing‑along Sugar Magnolia to close the night. The second set erupts with Truckin' leading straight into an expansive drum break before launching into a masterful Other One suite bookended by Me And My Uncle – a sequence that showcases Phil’s machine‑gun bass runs and Jerry’s confident improvisations. The band rides this momentum through Wharf Rat, wraps it up with a joyous Sugar Magnolia and caps the evening with a rollicking Johnny B. Goode encore. The Miller soundboard tape (gd71-11-14.sbd.miller.23568.sbeok.shnf) captures every nuance with crystal‑clear balance, making this one of the most listenable early‑’70 shows available.",
